I say one of the main villains because just
because one big bad is coming back doesn't

00:00:13.459 --> 00:00:15.500
mean others won't follow.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.619
So this video is going to be a breakdown of
the new footage and my top 5 theories about

00:00:18.619 --> 00:00:20.350
how Davros could still be alive.

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:23.920
Hello to any new people, if you're just finding
me for the first time, I'm doing weekly Doctor

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.019
Who videos until Series 8 gets here.

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:26.910
I'll be doing a ton of stuff during the season.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:31.820
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.520
So let's start with the actual footage.

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.700
What they've done in the last couple of teasers
is use the same scene from different perspectives.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.320
The TARDIS console erupting in Sparks.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.190
In the previous clip and that first image
they released The Doctor was standing away

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.310
from it, but in this he's operating the console.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.040
It's the same basic scene, just a different
moment inside it.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:53.190
The really interesting part comes after that
first explosion.

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:55.270
If you don't recognize the voice, it's Davros.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:00:59.290
I had to listen to it twice because the first
time my volume was turned down and it sounded

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:00.610
like a Dalek.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.370
Daleks have been confirmed for Series 8.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:08.960
The second time I heard it, the voice was
way too human to be a normal Dalek, and not

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:09.960
high pitched enough.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:15.549
And I re-listened to a clip from Davros' voice,
here's what the voice in the trailer sounds

00:01:15.549 --> 00:01:31.939
like....And here's what Davros' voice sounded
like during Stolen Earth in Series 4.

00:01:31.939 --> 00:01:36.740
So yes, Davros is back, we'll talk about the
mechanics of how he's back in a second.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.760
First let's finish talking about what he's
saying to The Doctor.

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:44.819
I see into your soul, I see beauty, divinity,
hatred.

00:01:44.819 --> 00:01:48.149
As he's saying these things it looks like
He's scanning the Doctor.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:49.890
As if he's inside the TARDIS with him.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:54.770
I don't think this is the case, Davros' voice
sounds so dream-like, I wonder if it's coming

00:01:54.770 --> 00:02:01.740
from some sort of netherspace, like when we
heard the Time Lord's voices coming through

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.630
the cracks in the Universe in the 50th Anniversary
Special.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:08.179
Davros sounds like he's speaking from somewhere
far away.

00:02:08.179 --> 00:02:11.770
Plus the scan zooms in on the Doctor's Hearts
and his heart beats.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.360
I think a couple of things are going on here.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.840
I don't think Davros is going to try and steal
the Doctor's body parts or anything.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.030
I think he's stuck without a body somewhere,
like outside the Universe.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.849
And he's going to play on the new Doctor's
personality to help him return.

00:02:24.849 --> 00:02:26.349
So how is he still alive?

00:02:26.349 --> 00:02:29.900
Well technically his final fate was never
confirmed after Journey's End.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:34.040
In that episode, the meta-crisis Doctor and
Donna were able to destroy the new Daleks

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.939
and left Davros on the Crucible which was
burning.

00:02:36.939 --> 00:02:41.439
He himself had been enslaved by the Supreme
Dalek and the new Daleks and forced to create

00:02:41.439 --> 00:02:42.930
the Reality Bomb.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:47.900
The Doctor offered to save him but Davros
said no and cursed the Doctor naming him the

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:49.299
Destroyer of Worlds.

00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:53.579
It was an interesting twist on the character
since Davros had been such a villain over

00:02:53.579 --> 00:02:54.579
the years.

00:02:54.579 --> 00:02:57.799
To be fair he started out as more of a misguided
mad scientist.

00:02:57.799 --> 00:03:01.810
Not a straight up monster villain.

00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:05.660
So it's pretty clear at this point he didn't
die and somehow used the Medusa Cascade to

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:06.689
survive.

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:10.670
Supposedly The Doctor sealed it in Journey's
End, but my guess is that the events of the

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:15.120
50th Anniversary and the cracks in the Universe
allowed Davros to send messages out.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:34.019
The dreamlike quality of his voice makes it
sound like he's still stuck 

00:03:34.019 --> 00:03:39.989
in there.

00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:44.950
In case you haven't seen any of the episodes
involving the Medusa Cascade it's a rift in

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.530
space time.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:50.870
The Daleks were going to use Davros' reality
bomb to cause an explosion that would travel

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.750
from the rift into normal space across all
Universes.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:56.230
Remember your multiverse theory.

00:03:56.230 --> 00:04:00.180
They were trying to make it so they would
be the only race left in existence.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:02.069
In any universe.

00:04:02.069 --> 00:04:07.390
So here are my top 5 theories about how Davros
could return during Series 8.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:11.610
Number 5 - He could have already used the
cracks in the universe to return and has been

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:15.749
rebuilding his power somewhere quietly since
the 50th Anniversary.

00:04:15.749 --> 00:04:21.530
Number 4 - Steven Moffat will bring back the
idea of Dalek Khan's prophecy and interpret

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:22.830
it in a new way.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:26.970
Davros' speech during Journey's End talked
about looking into the Doctor's Soul.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:30.780
That was all happening while Dalek Caan was
secretly manipulating events to help bring

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:33.009
about the destruction of his own race.

00:04:33.009 --> 00:04:38.400
Number 3 - He rebuilt part of the Crucible
and used it to get out.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.440
It's a simple re-purposing of the machinery.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:42.810
Number 2 - Davros will use something we haven't
seen yet, an alliance with a new character

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:44.150
to help him get out.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:50.590
Number 1 - He's still stuck inside the Medusa
Cascade and he's going to play on the Doctor's

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:55.700
personality to trick him into helping Davros
escape.

00:04:55.700 --> 00:05:00.820
The master was able to trick the Doctor using
the pocket watch, if he can do it, so could

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:01.820
Davros.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:09.780
They were just seen filming the final episodes
of series 8 featuring that new character called

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.100
The Gatekeeper and loads of Cybermen.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:16.610
Someone even spotted the head of a classic
Mondas Cyberman on the ground.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:21.120
So it's possible that Davros could return
right before or during the finale and The

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:25.220
Doctor will get the help of this new character
and the cybermen to help defeat him.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:29.850
The doesn't look like he's a captive of the
Cybermen in these pictures, that's why I'm

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.370
speculating they're helping him.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:34.539
It could be a situation like 'the enemy of
my enemy is my friend'.

00:05:34.539 --> 00:05:38.350
The Daleks and the Cybermen have worked together
in the past, but they're not friendly races.

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:43.410
And Davros' own Dalek creations even betrayed
him during Series 4, so alliances change all

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.410
the time.

